ere a tenant of any premises sublets them in contravention of the Rent Act and the premises are thereafter sold by the landlord to a 3`d party, the purchaser is entitled to maintain an action in ejectment of the tenant and the subtenant, is amply covered by authority and there is no dispute about that. See Rathnasingham Vs. Catheraswamy(1) and Thaha Vs. Sadeen(2). At the trial it was proved that t

